3. JENSEN, KELLY AND PEDERSEN (JKP) GLOBAL FACTOR DATA

Paths (series or statistics computed from JKP files):
  results/2026-09-factor-lab/sizing/returns.parquet  (columns RESMOM:*)
  results/2026-09-factor-lab/correlations/corr_*.csv (RESMOM and jkp:*)
  results/2026-09-factor-lab/*.json
  results/2026-09-factor-lab/sizing/summary.json
  results/2026-09-fundamentals/replication/*        (public|* columns)

Source: https://jkpfactors.com/ (factor files fetched from its download
links; URLs and hashes in results/2026-09-factor-lab/sources.json and the
registrations under registrations/).

Terms: CC BY-NC 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
  https://jkpfactors.com/ and https://jkpfactors.com/data, page footer:
  "Data is licensed under CC BY-NC 4.0." and "Analysis code is available
  under the MIT License."
The licence does not permit commercial use, and the MIT grant does not extend
to these series. Whether trading real money with a configuration evaluated
against them counts as commercial use is not decided here.

Attribution: the site asks, "Please cite our paper if you are using this
data": Jensen, T. I., B. Kelly and L. H. Pedersen (2023), "Is There a
Replication Crisis in Finance?", The Journal of Finance 78(5), 2465-2518.


